Z||000000||FieroJoe||02-23-2001||09:24 PM||||Alrighty, after reading about the positive and negative backpressure EGR's from the topic ChadMan started, I decided to go check mine.  For some odd reason, I still had the old one laying around (probably didnt want to throw it away if it wasn't the source of the problem I was trying to fix), and both the one that was in the car and the new one that has been in it for about 3000 miles had POS stamped on it.<P>what gives?  Shouldn't I be having any negative effects from this?  though I have not driven the car since late october (torn down for resto.), I had no driveability problems at all.  I believe that the old EGR valve I took out was probably installed by a GM service shop, from the previous owner.<P>So any ideas whether I should throw away my $50 POS (not piece of sh*t... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) EGR and get the correct AC Delco (negative backpressure) one?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||02-24-2001||12:23 AM||||OK, now I'm really confused.<P>Went to the garage to get the book to read up on this + and - stuff... Haynes and 88 Pontiac manual both say 4 cyl has Neg EGR. While I was out there I happened to notice the 84 has POS on it (Came from NAPA). It's not running now, but when it was running it was pretty much OK.. it did have some pinging and some funny idle issues from time to time though... I didn't drive it much after the new EGR either, so it's hard to say for sure... hmmm...<P>The description of operation seems like they both accomplish the same results from the opposite directions... Pos opens it when there is positive exhaust pressure... Neg closes it when there is negative exhaust pressure...<P>Mine is cat-less too. I'm guessing that would make for less exhaust back pressure and effect the operation.<P>Why are the stores giving us POS valves?<BR>Should either work?<BR>How will less restricted exhaust affect EGR operation?<P>Ogre, HELP!!! This is starting to look like a Unicorn!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||02-24-2001||06:15 PM||||Actually I think they open when vacuum is applied to them.  To tell that my old one was bad, I felt under the valve to where I could feel the diaphragm.  As you revv the engine, the diaphragm should open proportionatly, from the intake manifold vacuum.  Well it didnt so that is why I replaced it.<P>So I got the new one, and it worked as it should.  very weird that we're getting POS valves instead of negative ones.||||reg||1
